From: TRASC Android project
Subject: [PATCH] server: allow translated Unix process cleanup to finish

Wine marks the Windows process exited before Box64/PRoot finish Unix cleanup.
A kernel trace on ARM64 identifies wineserver's ~0.5s timer as the SIGKILL
sender after the Windows fixture called exit(0). Allow approximately 8s,
covering Box64's existing 5s native-exit watchdog, while retaining the bounded
SIGKILL fallback. Windows exit codes, process handles and running-game behavior
are unchanged. TRASC's owned Stop still has its independent forced cleanup.

--- a/server/process.c
+++ b/server/process.c
@@ -615,3 +615,3 @@
     process->sigkill_delay *= 2;
-    if (process->sigkill_delay >= TICKS_PER_SEC / 2)
+    if (process->sigkill_delay >= TICKS_PER_SEC * 8)
         signal = SIGKILL;
